    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "`AcceptanceTest` is the only test class, and the suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented the soft-duplicate (\"possible duplicate\") rule for `POST /api/owners`. A new owner that isn't a hard duplicate but shares an existing owner's `lastName` + `postcode` with a *different* telephone is still created, and is flagged `possibleDuplicate: true` / `possibleDuplicateOf: <matching id>` (otherwise `possibleDuplicate: false`, `possibleDuplicateOf` absent).\n\nChanges, kept as small cohesive units:\n\n- **`FlagPossibleDuplicate.java`** (new) \u2014 a one-method OfficeFloor step mirroring `AssignNamesakeCount`: scans pre-existing owners for a matching `lastName` (case-insensitive) + `postcode` with a different telephone, and records the match id via `owner.setPossibleDuplicateOf(...)`. New class, so zero surrounding complexity.\n- **`owners.POST.yml`** \u2014 wired the step in after `assignNamesakeCount`, before `save`, under the same `transaction` governance.\n- **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added the persisted `possibleDuplicateOf` field with a plain getter/setter (the `possibleDuplicate` boolean is derived, not stored).\n- **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 one `@Mapping` expression for the derived `possibleDuplicate` boolean; `possibleDuplicateOf` maps automatically by name. This makes both the POST response and later GET carry the flags.\n- **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the two read-only `Owner` schema properties (regenerates the DTO).\n- **`db/hsqldb/schema.sql`** + **`data.sql`** \u2014 added the `possible_duplicate_of` column and padded the positional seed inserts.\n\nI limited the DB change to the hsqldb dialect (the only one the tests use, and the only one already carrying the other derived-field columns like `namesake_count`/`household_id`); the h2/mysql/postgres schemas are already out of sync with those features, so I left them as-is rather than touch extra files.\n\nBoth the new acceptance test and the full suite are green (`BUILD SUCCESS`).",
